    {
      "id": "ydb0f4y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.2.2 Binary to Decimal Conversion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ssafyp1",
      "content": "Multiply each binary digit by powers of 2 and add the results."
    },
    {
      "id": "niacyud",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.2.3 Binary to Octal Conversion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u2z6d7w",
      "content": "Group binary digits into sets of three bits from right to left."
    },
    {
      "id": "9iv2t7w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.2.4 Binary to Hexadecimal Conversion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vysa86u",
      "content": "Group binary digits into sets of four bits from right to left."
    },
    {
      "id": "iewb7at",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.3 ASCII (American Standard Code for Information Interchange)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rvddsd4",
      "content": "ASCII is a character encoding standard used to represent text in computers."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "In Hexadecimal system, letters A to F represent values 10 to 15 respectively.",
        "Converting Binary to Octal requires grouping binary bits into groups of 3 from right to left.",
        "Converting Binary to Hexadecimal requires grouping binary bits into groups of 4 from right to left.",
        "Full expansion of ASCII is frequently asked in competitive computer awareness sections."
      ],
      "id": "6cknn36"
    },
